  "scout_brief": "arXMCP wants execution-based verification feedback for its downstream sketcher -> autoformalizer -> tactician -> fixer pipeline. Two seed ideas motivate this scout: (1) expose a Lean kernel verification-trace MCP tool so the tactician -> fixer loop receives real execution feedback (compile/typecheck/proof-state output) rather than only retrieved grounding context; (2) wire up the cite_neighbors MCP tool -- the handler in server/handlers/citations.py is a known v1 stub (CLAUDE.md section 7) while the underlying server/graph_queries.py library is real. Scout broadly around these themes: execution-feedback and verification surfaces an MCP retrieval server can expose to an autoformalization agent, and closing the citation-graph proof-chain tool gap. Surface adjacent capabilities too -- do not limit findings to only these two.",
